var update_default = "---\nlayout: article\ntitle: Update a rule\ndescription: Change an existing Appwrite Firewall rule's name, scope, conditions, action settings, priority, or enabled state.\n---\n\nYou can update Firewall rules from the rules list without recreating them. Changes apply to new requests after save. Historical metrics are not rewritten.\n\n# Open update {% #open-update %}\n\n1. Open **Firewall** in your project.\n2. Select the **API**, **Functions**, or **Sites** tab that contains the rule.\n3. Open the rule's actions menu and choose **Update**, or use the update action from the rule context menu.\n\n# What you can change {% #what-you-can-change %}\n\n| Field | Notes |\n|-------|-------|\n| Name and description | Labels only; no traffic impact |\n| Resource type and resource ID | Move the rule between API, Functions, and Sites (pick a function or site when required) |\n| Conditions | Rebuilt with the same condition builder as create; at least one complete condition required |\n| Rate limit settings | Request limit, interval, and limit by when the rule action is rate limit. Token-bucket rules can also change **Max bucket size**. |\n| Redirect settings | Location and status code (`300`–`399`) when the rule action is redirect |\n| Priority | `-100000` to `100000`; lower numbers evaluated first |\n| Enabled | Disable to pause without deleting |\n\nThe **action type** (deny, bypass, challenge, rate limit, redirect) is set at create time and cannot be changed on update. To switch actions, [create a new rule](/docs/products/firewall/create) and [delete](/docs/products/firewall/delete) the old one.\n\nA rate limit rule's **[strategy](/docs/products/firewall/actions#rate-limit-strategies)** (`fixedWindow`, `slidingWindow`, or `tokenBucket`) is likewise fixed at create time and cannot be changed on update — the Console shows it as read-only. To move a rule to a different strategy, recreate it. **Max bucket size** remains editable on token-bucket rules.\n\n# Safe updates {% #safe-updates %}\n\nWhen tightening a deny or rate limit:\n\n1. Review the impact preview if shown while editing conditions.\n2. Consider lowering match breadth (narrower path, exact IP, or tighter CIDR range) before increasing severity.\n3. Prefer **disable** temporarily if you need to stop a rule during an incident, then fix conditions and re-enable.\n\nWhen adding an allowlist:\n\n1. Create or update a **bypass** rule with the trusted IP or path.\n2. Give it a **lower priority number** than the deny or rate limit it should override. See [Priority](/docs/products/firewall/priority).\n\nRemember that a matching **rate limit** under quota also stops later rules, same as bypass.\n\n# Save {% #save %}\n\nConfirm the update in the drawer. On success, the list reflects the new values. If update fails, the previous rule configuration remains active.\n\n{% arrow_link href=\"/docs/products/firewall/monitor\" %}\nMonitor traffic\n{% /arrow_link %}\n";
export { update_default as default };
